        10["<div style='font-weight: bold'>AUTO</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The AUTO button (formerly<br />Perfect): while held (and no<br />sheet or dialog is up, and<br />the player isn't steering,<br />gathering or working a tile)<br />it asks the brain for the<br />next intent about four times<br />a second and has the<br />Controller carry it out, the<br />same calls a tap makes. Keeps<br />the badge (what it's doing),<br />waits at Embark with a toast,<br />and keeps the screen awake<br />while held.</div>"]
        style 10 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        11["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Camera</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Maps world (x, y, height) to<br />screen pixels and back<br />(project/unproject) with zoom<br />and a fixed slight lean;<br />picking hits the top or face<br />you see. Also the visible<br />tile range.</div>"]
        style 11 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        12["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Renderer</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Paints all floor tiles before<br />standing objects in<br />north-to-south row order.<br />Local viewport-bounded masks<br />preserve higher foreground<br />terrain occlusion without<br />clipping feet against<br />equal-height floor. The faint<br />visibility pass omits<br />character and boat shadows;<br />placement ghosts share the<br />masks, Wiki focus and map<br />mode retain their independent<br />paths, and renderer fault<br />recovery restores canvas<br />clipping. The default player<br />is Mica, a compact flat<br />orange-hooded repairer with<br />skinned split coat/patch,<br />explicit-time mesh-eye blinks<br />and curious idle/recovery<br />poses, actual-cargo<br />protective carrying and<br />localized inspection, with<br />eight snapped world headings:<br />twenty-one bone hierarchy<br />with four weighted cloak<br />panels, one-handed mining<br />from the shaft's end and<br />fixed-length arm IK to the<br />WORK_HANDS targets in<br />work-motion.js, earned<br />palm-bound baskets and belt<br />lanterns from<br />work-equipment.js, free-hand<br />assembly and a one-cycle<br />coalescing actor queue with<br />captured work facing, torso<br />and head counterbalance,<br />articulated elbows and<br />wrists, and pure two-bone leg<br />IK plus layered action curves<br />from rig-motion.js.<br />rig-model.js builds the rig<br />without a renderer and names<br />its solids and their joints<br />and grips; rig-clips.js finds<br />crossing triangles between<br />them, which the unit sweep<br />and the local dev build treat<br />as a fault.<br />rigged-character.js lazily<br />bundles vendored Three.js and<br />reuses one 320x448 WebGL<br />surface composited into the<br />2D canvas. Wiki, a four-bone<br />mycelium sprite with a<br />skinned folding cap<br />(wiki-model.js, pure pose in<br />wiki-motion.js), rides the<br />hood bone in the same pass<br />and outline; src/game/wiki.js<br />decides what it looks at and<br />says (a long press on the map<br />asks it), and focus.js rings<br />what it talks about in Wiki<br />teal around the whole object.<br />pickaxe-model.js supplies<br />cached six-tier palm/back<br />equipment and offline-baked<br />matching icons, one flat fill<br />mesh per tier with no ink<br />shell; the character contour<br />outlines it while equipped<br />and a 2D silhouette stamp<br />outlines the icons.<br />Action/boat feedback shares<br />canonical timing;<br />presentation never runs<br />simulation ticks. Mica is not<br />drawn while the rig loads;<br />without WebGL and for<br />friends, the 2D wanderer<br />stands in. A cached<br />multisampled color target and<br />one alpha-derived<br />screen-space ink pass outline<br />the complete figure,<br />replacing per-piece hulls.<br />Exact sRGB fills are<br />preserved, with no CPU<br />readback in normal rendering.<br />Geometry, combined-pass draw<br />calls and compressed module<br />size are bounded.<br />resource-models.js builds<br />four canonical 3D materials<br />and offline vector views<br />through<br />scripts/resource-art.mjs;<br />icons/deposits/small piles<br />remain cached texture-pack<br />SVGs at runtime, flat value<br />planes over one whole-object<br />ink silhouette with no face<br />or part edges. No player<br />text.</div>"]
        style 12 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        13["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Effects</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Particles, floating text and<br />flyers (resources homing into<br />the pack), with budgets and a<br />flyer lifetime so bursts stay<br />cheap.</div>"]
        style 13 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        14["<div style='font-weight: bold'>HUD and Sheet</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Resource chips and rates, the<br />depth marker, the contextual<br />thumb buttons, the message<br />log (everything the game and<br />Wiki say, kept per world on<br />the device until the player<br />folds it away), and the<br />bottom sheet: the Progression<br />map (family rails over the<br />upgrade registry), Build,<br />Beyond and the earnings<br />statement (income per<br />building with charts kept per<br />world, payback, best buys,<br />spending), with NEW on Build<br />and Upgrade until what became<br />affordable is looked at; the<br />phone's Back steps back<br />through it. Keeps normal play<br />concise; delegated<br />hover/focus and passive touch<br />inspection reuse localized<br />catalog descriptions,<br />rejecting unexplored cells<br />before indexed world lookup.</div>"]
        style 14 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        15["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Audio</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>A small WebAudio synth<br />unlocked by the first<br />gesture: per-material gather<br />voices,<br />collect/build/upgrade/fanfare<br />cues and an extractor hum.<br />Takes parameters, never reads<br />game state.</div>"]
        style 15 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        16["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Look</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>What everything looks like:<br />the game's one pack<br />(packs/default/). Loads and<br />rasterises its pictures per<br />size, picks variants and<br />animation frames. An<br />unavailable essential startup<br />pack fails with picture/URL<br />details. HTML pictures never<br />emit empty URLs: missing<br />IDs/slots keep labels/layout<br />with a placeholder and a<br />structured fault. Optional<br />DOM resource errors remain<br />nonfatal, with bounded<br />pre-boot queuing and<br />element/request/catalog/build/HTTP<br />diagnostics carried into<br />Problems with world context<br />and map-tap breadcrumbs. Card<br />picture-slot and actual Geode<br />mouse-click tests guard the<br />path. Drawing code and the<br />HUD ask it for colours and<br />pictures by thing id; players<br />cannot load their own.</div>"]
        style 16 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        17["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Yard</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Keeps the stockpile's layout<br />in step with the inventory<br />(at most five times a<br />second), tracks which tiles<br />big piles cover, and makes<br />changes visible like 2048:<br />ten piles slide together into<br />the bigger one they became,<br />moved piles slide, new piles<br />grow in, spent piles puff.</div>"]
        style 17 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        18["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Storage</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript + localStorage]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Guarded localStorage: load,<br />save (reporting failures,<br />never over another tab's<br />save) and setting aside a<br />save it can't read rather<br />than writing over it, plus<br />per-browser view settings.<br />All solo collection models<br />share normal saves, backup<br />imports and per-seed<br />archives. Earlier depot keys<br />remain read-only recovery<br />sources; incompatible<br />local-collection worlds do<br />not connect to rooms.</div>"]
        style 18 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        19["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Together</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript + WebSocket]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Playing together<br />(src/game/together.js): joins<br />a shared world from a QR link<br />(#join=room.invite) or opens<br />a moderator's copy of one<br />(#copy=room.key;<br />src/game/copy.js keeps the<br />browser's storage in memory<br />then), relays your position,<br />world edits and progress to<br />the room and applies what it<br />sends after checking it<br />(src/net/protocol.js). Keeps<br />friends and their states<br />(online, away, connection<br />lost, offline) for the<br />renderer and the HUD chips,<br />and makes the QR code for the<br />sign your wanderer holds up<br />in the world<br />(src/vendor/qrcode.js). The<br />worlds you've been in, their<br />generated names and the<br />Worlds screen that switches<br />between them are in<br />src/game/worlds.js; the<br />friend chips and the Players<br />screen (everyone in the<br />world) are drawn by<br />src/game/players.js.</div>"]
        style 19 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        20["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Sync</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript + HTTPS]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Your own world on every<br />device you link<br />(src/game/sync.js): the<br />device that shows the QR on<br />the Another device screen<br />(src/game/devices.js) makes a<br />secret sync key, the one that<br />opens its link (#link=key)<br />takes it. Each keeps the<br />world it plays in the room<br />service's vault while it's<br />played and takes the newest<br />when it comes to the front;<br />the world played last carries<br />on, and only when both played<br />the same world does the<br />which-world question come up<br />(src/game/fork.js). Brings a<br />world back to a browser that<br />forgot it.</div>"]
        style 20 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        5["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Main Loop</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Wires the modules together<br />and owns the current state<br />(game.state, replaced on<br />embark/reset). Schedules the<br />shared fixed-tick engine<br />independently of drawing.<br />Each simulation tick steers,<br />steps the Core, reveals fog,<br />works held input and ticks<br />AUTO; presentation separately<br />updates effects, save/HUD<br />timers and rendering. A<br />frame, a drawing layer or a<br />tap that throws is skipped<br />and kept as a problem report<br />(faults.js, problems.js);<br />only frames failing in a row<br />stop the game. Exposes<br />window.MTE_GAME for the<br />browser tests.</div>"]
        style 5 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        6["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Tick and Deadline Engine</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Shared 60 Hz logical clock.<br />Browser catch-up is bounded;<br />the headless runner coalesces<br />stationary ticks ending at<br />AUTO/goal deadlines,<br />retaining fine motion and<br />first Embark eligibility.<br />Cumulative battery intervals<br />preserve daylight<br />transitions. Injected<br />controller, AUTO and input<br />interfaces keep scheduling<br />independent of presentation.<br />Blocked UI suspends<br />AUTO-owned movement.</div>"]
        style 6 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        7["<div style='font-weight: bold'>AUTO Developer Viewer</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Lazy single-player viewer<br />booted before normal world<br />loading. Lazily loads<br />viewer-only styles and<br />labels. Runs the shipped AUTO<br />session in bounded real-time<br />work slices at selectable<br />speed, renders the normal<br />client view, and retains<br />separate IndexedDB worlds.<br />The evaluation runner imports<br />the same session.</div>"]
        style 7 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        8["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Input</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Raw touch/mouse/keyboard to<br />intents: drag-anywhere<br />joystick, tap, hold Gather<br />(button or Space), hold AUTO<br />(button or P), the Trail<br />stroke (hold Gather and<br />draw), pinch/wheel/button<br />zoom, and sheet shortcuts.<br />Holds no game state; calls<br />the handlers it is given.</div>"]
        style 8 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        9["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Controller</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Applies intents to the game:<br />tap (descend, harvest,<br />collect, or walk there round<br />obstacles: planWalk/walkAim<br />in core paths.js, replanned<br />when a hoped-open route<br />through fog turns out<br />blocked), Gather (collect,<br />else harvest, else Explore<br />walks to the nearest<br />resource) and its hold,<br />AUTO's intents (perform),<br />Trail sweeps (every way of<br />working a tile takes turns on<br />one hand clock, core<br />pace.js), going down and up<br />between layers, buying,<br />building, embarking,<br />resetting. Each calls the<br />Core, then triggers effects,<br />sound, HUD and a save.</div>"]
        style 9 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
      end

      21["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Pictures</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: JSON + SVG]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Lanternlight<br />(packs/default/): pack.json<br />mapping every thing in the<br />Catalog to its SVG pictures<br />and colours. Required before<br />the game draws anything; unit<br />tests check it against the<br />Catalog.</div>"]
      style 21 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
      24["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Simulation Core</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: JavaScript modules (browser + Node)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The game rules (src/core/).<br />Pure and deterministic: no<br />DOM, no clock, no<br />Math.random. Terrain is a<br />pure function of (x, y, z,<br />seed), state is a plain<br />object, and the same modules<br />run in the browser and in<br />Node tests.</div>"]
      style 24 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
